<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19131" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fūruncŭlus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		dim.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				petty thief</i>, <i>pilferer</i> (cf. furax).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">olim furunculus, nunc etiam rapax,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 27, 66</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 3,
			16</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A pointed</i>, <i>burning sore on the
				human body</i>, <i>a boil</i>, <i>furuncle</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 5, 28, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 20,
				13, 50, § 130</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A germ</i> or <i>knob on a vine</i>,
			so called from its shape, <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 22, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 24, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 17,
				22, 36, § 181</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>